ulty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS Programs, Majors College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Academic Catalog Academic Resources Research Registrar ADMISSIONS Apply, Financial Aid Apply Now Requirements Campus Visit Open House Financial Assistance Scholarships Net Price Calculator Accepted Students Orientation Honors Graduate Programs Dual Enrollment School Counselors Request Information ATHLETICS Sports, Events STUDENT LIFE Activities, Events Activities & Organizations Student Health Greek Life Ms. FMU Housing Available Positions Human Resources Policies Available Positions Professional Development Excellent Career opportunities Promoting diversity in the workplace As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, we especially welcome applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission. Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in South Carolina. Francis Marion University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution. For more information on any position, or for general information on employment at FMU, please contact us at (843) 661-1140 . Keywords Location Remote positions only Category Any category Biology Campus Police Department Enrollment Management Admissions Finance and Facilities Facilities Management Custodian Gail and Terry Richardson Center for the Child Human Resources Provost Office School of Education School of Health Sciences Nursing Speech-Language P