      "description": "Benefits and Leave Coordinator (26-48) - Francis Marion University Potential Students Campus Tours and Maps Campus Map Student Life Accounting for Students Apply Now Dining Services Financial Assistance Graduate Programs Honors Housing International Programs Majors Scholarships Visit Registrar Current Students Student Resources Blackboard Campus Technology CASA Career Center CASA Advising Tutoring Center Writing Center Testing, Counseling, & Special Services Center Dining Services Disability Services Purchase Textbooks Rogers Library Ombudsman Student Handbook Student Services and Documents Registrar’s Office Accounting Bookstore Calendar Course Catalogs Directory Financial Assistance Honors Housing Patriot Gear Patriot Marketplace Registrar Scholarships Student Employment Student Life SwampFox Alerts Alumni Alumni Gear Give Donate Homecoming Join News Alumni Magazine Community Calendar Campus Tours and Maps Evening College Facility Rental Foundation & Development Economic Development Education Foundation Freshwater Ecology Complex Gately Gallery Hewn Timber Cabins Kelley Center Performing Arts Center Regional & Community Programs Richardson Center for the Child Dooley Planetarium University Communications FOIA Requests Faculty/Staff African American Faculty & Staff Coalition Blackboard Calendar Campus Technology Career Opportunities Directory Email Facilities Management Space Reservation Faculty Handbook Grants Human Resources Employment Opportunities Policies Library Performing Arts Center Richardson Center for the Child SwampFox Alerts Patriot Portal Password Management- Reset & Recovery Portal 101 Portal Login Proxy Login Authorized User Login Career Opportunities Menu APPLY Apply to FMU Apply Now ABOUT History, Facts President Campus Tours and Maps Administration Policies Human Resources Facilities Management Financial Services & Budget Office University Communications Registrar General Counsel Foundation & Development Institutional Research Staff Awards Faculty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS Programs, Majors College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Academic Catalog Academic Resources Research Registrar ADMISSIONS Apply, Financial Aid Apply Now Requirements Campus Visit Open House Financial Assistance Scholarships Net Price Calculator Accepted Students Orientation Honors Graduate Programs Dual Enrollment School Counselors Request Information ATHLETICS Sports, Events STUDENT LIFE Activities, Events Activities & Organizations Student Health Greek Life Ms. FMU Housing Benefits and Leave Coordinator (26-48) Home job July 21, 2026 Benefits and Leave Coordinator (26-48) Full-Time Staff Stokes Administration Building Posted 2 months ago Francis Marion University and the Department of Human Resources invite applications for a Benefits and Leave Coordinator who will assist with the creation of personnel records for new staff members; update the records of existing staff; have thorough knowledge of Employee Benefits programs and Leave programs; maintain records and reports associated with each program; understand the Fair Labor Standards Act as it pertains to compensation and classification; and provide professional technical assistance in the coordination of human resource programs in the HR department. Other responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Assists the Associate Director of Human Resources-Employee Services with Leave and Benefits Programs, maintenance of staff records, and Worker’s Compensation cases. Provides the Associate Director of Human Resources-Administrative Services with the time, leave information necessary to run payroll and complete the required reports. Maintains Time Records for all full-time non-exempt employees. Conducts orientation to acquaint new staff with agency policies, procedures, and regulations concerning Benefits and Leave. Describes insurance and retirement benefits, and other benefits as available, to new and existing employees. Discusses eligibility for insurance coverage under the Affordable Care Act. Ensures that staff are enrolled in his/her selected programs. Assist staff in using websites provided by the Public Employee Benefits Administration. Consults with supervisors to ensure that adequate records are maintained for hours worked, and leave used. Provides this information to other HR staff as required. Reviews staff leave records with the employee and supervisor, as needed. Coordinates with supervisor, employee, and HR staff, if necessary, when situations requiring extended leave arise (e.g., FMLA). Coordinates with supervisor and staff member–and HR staff, if necessary—when abuse of leave is suspected. Assists in compliance with Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA)  requirements. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Required: Knowledge of Human Resources principles (i.e., hiring, good employee relations, disciplinary practices, end of employment). Ability to quickly acquire working knowledge of federal laws and state regulations affecting human resources ( FMLA, FLSA, ACA ). Proficient in Microsoft Office products such as Word, Excel, Outlook and 365. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships. Ability to analyze needs and to recommend and communicate solutions effectively. Bachelor’s Degree in any field and experience in Human Resources. Or Bachelor’s Degree in Human Resources. Applicants without degrees will be considered if they have records of employment which indicate the existence of the requisite knowledge, skills and abilities . Preference: Experience with an Enterprise Resource Planning software system (e.g. Colleague, Banner, Oracle). State Classification: Human Resources Coordinator (AG07) Fed Category: E2 Pay Grade: GEN08 Salary: $46,206 Materials Needed: Letter of Interest (Referencing Position Number 26-48 ). Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate). Resume. The names, addresses, and telephone numbers of three references; and FMU Staff Application. To obtain the FMU Staff Application, please click here. Send Application Packet to: Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University, PO Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547 or FAX to (843) 661-1202. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission. Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC. An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution July 21, 2026 | | APPLY Ready to start your FMU journey? Apply now CONTACT Get in touch with a friendly FMU representative. VISIT Schedule an in-person tour or View the Campus map here . DONATE Give the gift of opportunity to a Francis Marion Patriot here. IMPORTANT LINKS FMU Safe Campus Tucker Hipps Report Title IX & Discrimination Policies Clery Report Transparency Reports Student Achievement & Success Website Privacy GDPR Policy Campus Map Accreditation UNIVERSITY HONORS U.S. News & World Report Best Social Mobility U.S. News & World Report Best Regional University South U.S. News & World Report Top Public University U.S. News & World Report Top Performer Economic Diversity U.S. News & World Report Top Business & Engineering Schools TOP © 2026 Francis Marion University | 4822 E. Palmetto