ds Faculty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS Programs, Majors College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Academic Catalog Academic Resources Research Registrar ADMISSIONS Apply, Financial Aid Apply Now Requirements Campus Visit Open House Financial Assistance Scholarships Net Price Calculator Accepted Students Orientation Honors Graduate Programs Dual Enrollment School Counselors Request Information ATHLETICS Sports, Events STUDENT LIFE Activities, Events Activities & Organizations Student Health Greek Life Ms. FMU Housing Trades Specialist (26-28) Home job January 26, 2026 Trades Specialist (26-28) Full-Time Staff Facilities Posted 7 months ago Francis Marion University invites applications for a Trades Specialist who, under general supervision, performs skilled duties involved in the maintenance, repair, and modification of buildings and equipment. Other responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Installs, repairs, or replaces building components, including locks, door closers, windows, glass, walls, and other sections thereof, masonry, carpet, tile, vinyl tile, light fixtures, ballasts, bulbs, toilets, sheetrock railings, roofs, and miscellaneous other elements of buildings and items of equipment. Surveys job requirements and requests parts, tools, equipment, and/or materials needed. Assists other craftsmen or, to the extent of their own expertise, accomplishes necessary tasks in maintenance and repairs of plumbing, electrical systems, and carpentry related items. Properly prepares and paints elements of buildings and items of equipment. Troubleshoots, repairs, and installs locks, door closures, and panic bars. Can respond to facilities problems during other than normal working hours, earning overtime; may serve as primary person on call on a rotating basis earning overtime. State Requirements: Formal training or trades experience that is directly related to the area of employment. Some positions require a commercial driver’s license. Some positions require certification or licensure. FMU Preferences: High School graduate with 3-5 years’ work experience directly related to the area of employment.  A trade course would be helpful but not required.  Desirable skills but not required: plumbing, welding masonry, concrete work, rough carpentry, framing, drywall construction, painting, etc.  Must be able to see well enough to read chemical labels accurately in various lighting conditions and to operate equipment safely at normal sound cues from other traffic and from equipment being operated. *Must have a valid SC Drivers License. Normal Working Hours: Monday-Friday 9:00am- 5:00pm. Summer Hours will vary. State Classification: Trades Specialist III,  KC30 Pay Grade: GEN06 Salary: $37,944 Materials Needed: 1. Letter of Interest (Referencing Position Number 26-28 ). 2. Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate). 3. Resume. 4. The names, addresses, email addresses, and telephone numbers of three references; and 5. FMU Staff Application To obtain the FMU Staff Application, please click here . Send Application Packet to: Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University, PO Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547 or FAX to (843) 661-1202. As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission. Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC. An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution January 26, 2026 | | APPLY Ready to start your FMU journey? Apply now CONTACT Get in touch with a friendly FMU representative. VISIT Schedule an in-person tour or View the Campus map here . DONATE Give the gift of opportunity to a Francis Marion Patriot here. IMPORTANT LINKS FMU Safe Campus Tucker Hipps Report Title IX & Discrimination Policies Clery Report Transparency Reports Student Achievement & Success Website Privacy GDPR Policy Campus Map Accreditation UNIVERSITY HONORS U.S. News & World Report Best Social Mobility U.S. News & World Report Best Regional University South U.S. News & World Report Top Public University U.S. News & World Report Top Performer Economic Diversity U.S. News & World Report Top Business & Engineering Schools TOP © 2026 Francis Marion University | 4822 E. Palmetto St., Florence, S.C. 29506 | PO Box 100547, Florence, S.C. 29502 APPLY Apply Now ABOUT President Campus Tours and Maps Administration Policies Human Resources Facilities Management Financial Services & Budget Office University Communications Registrar General Counsel Foundation & Development Institutional Research Staff Awards Faculty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Academic Catalog Academic Resources Research Registrar ADMISSIONS Apply Now Requirements Campus Visit Open House Financial Assistance Scholarships Net Price Calculator Accepted Students Orientation Honors Graduate Programs Dual Enrollment School Counselors Request Information ATHLETICS STUDENT LIFE Acti